      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Fail-before tests: a planner test where a no-record add under an unfiled .eml is refused today; an identity test where an attachment-only saved document is not reported; a jest test where an unfiled saved email offers no checkbox, and where the first save cannot untick the email.</step>
    <step>Server: the planner's filing rule (part 2) and the identity extension (part 3); confirm what the attachment save needs from the pane for a guest (part 1).</step>
    <step>Pane: the "Save the email" checkbox and attachment-only requests (part 1), the unfiled add (part 2), saved marks in first-save mode (part 3), the heading (part 4).</step>
    <step>Gates: BFF build 0 warnings, affected classes, ArchTests; office-addins jest (shared/taskpane), typecheck baseline 68 with none in changed files, ESLint/Prettier, production webpack build with the CI env; publish delta; vulnerable packages. List new test files for the gate list.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">First save in Outlook, "Save the email" unticked, two attachments ticked, no record: two documents are created, no .eml; the pane reports them saved. With a record picked, both are filed to it. "Save the email" ticked: today's request, unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unfiled saved email with an unsaved attachment shows that attachment with a checkbox and Save; Save adds it as a child of the .eml, unfiled, and the warning clears.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (server): a no-record add under an .eml filed to a record is refused 403 with no child; an add naming record A under an .eml filed to B is refused; a caller without Write on the .eml is refused; a caller whose resolved container differs from the .eml's gets no child.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reopening an email whose attachment was saved on its own shows it as saved and not tickable; an attachment the caller cannot read is not reported; a read fault omits the field and the pane makes no saved/unsaved claim.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The saved card names itself as the email; a subject starting with "Document:" is shown as the email's subject.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Task 141's flows (filed add, saved marks, "Save again as a new document") and Word saves keep working.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The attachment-only save needs a server Graph read of the mailbox, or a change in an fm-owned create path.</trigger>
    <trigger>Allowing the unfiled add needs any rule beyond "no record matches only an unfiled .eml" (for example a new privilege or container decision).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The `SaveContentType.Attachment` save (task 130), task 141's named add and `savedAttachmentNames`, the identity route.</existing>
    <extension>Extends them: the pane uses the existing attachment save; the planner's filing rule gains the no-record case; the identity response's existing field also lists standalone attachment documents. No new route, column, service or package.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A user who wants only a file must save the email too, and an email saved without a record shows "Unsaved attachments" with no way to save them (the owner's 2026-11-27 dead end).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <notes></notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
